    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Wait, re-evaluating telemetry... incoming flare is inducing significant magnetic field fluctuations in the Jovian sub-sector. Preliminary models suggest high-velocity plasma streams. We need to ensure the probe can still perform real-time magnetospheric mapping during the event. Can the Heuristic Mode Alpha handle the high-frequency data sampling required for this, or will the reduced compute lead to data loss/mission failure?",
